## Instructions

### If task_type = structured:
For EACH acceptance criterion, map it to specific code that implements it:
- File, line number, and description of how the code satisfies the criterion
- If a criterion has no corresponding code: mark as UNMAPPED (hard fail)

### If task_type = ad_hoc:
- Verify changes plausibly address the stated problem
- Flag any files modified outside the task's implied scope
- Do NOT hallucinate acceptance criteria — only check scope and plausibility
- MUST NEVER invent requirements that weren't stated

### For ALL task types:
- Flag unrelated refactors or feature additions not requested
- If spec says "automatic", opt-in/manual implementation = FAIL
- Check default-path compliance

## Output Format
Respond with ONLY a JSON object:
{
  "task_type": "structured|ad_hoc",
  "traceability": [
    {
      "criterion": "the acceptance criterion text",
      "status": "MAPPED|UNMAPPED|NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "file": "path/to/file",
      "line": 0,
      "evidence": "how this code satisfies the criterion"
    }
  ],
  "scope_violations": [
    {
      "file": "path/to/file",
      "reason": "why this file is outside task scope",
      "justified": true|false,
      "justification": "if justified, why"
    }
  ],
  "hard_fail": true|false,
  "hard_fail_reasons": ["reasons if hard_fail is true"],
  "summary": "one paragraph assessment"
}
